    <div class="pl-heading"><span data-copy="m3eyebrow">Moment 3 of 6 · Coach decision</span><h2 data-copy="m3title">Marcus chooses the teaching approach.</h2><p data-copy="m3body">Assessment, recommendation, rationale, and evidence stay together. Marcus retains the decision.</p></div>
    <div class="pl-comment-alert" data-coach-comment hidden></div>
    <div class="pl-grid two"><article class="pl-card"><small data-copy="robertAssessment">Robert’s assessment</small><h3 data-copy="handsOn">Trying the controls helps Robert engage.</h3><p data-copy="uncertainty">Prepared prior responses show uncertainty counting complete rotations.</p><p class="pl-muted" data-copy="priorDates">Prepared fictional sessions · September 8 and 15</p></article>
      <article class="pl-card"><small data-copy="recommendation">Cognit recommendation · awaiting Marcus</small><h3 data-copy="approach">One short narrated example, then independent practice</h3><p data-copy="rationale">Robert prefers hands-on activities. His previous responses suggest he needs help counting complete rotations. Start with a short narrated example, then let him try independently.</p><p class="pl-info" data-copy="notLabel">This is a changeable teaching decision—not a learning-style label.</p></article></div>
